From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:19:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: support hardware buffers over a host-allocation blob

Venus only offers the Android hardware buffer handle type when the renderer
advertises VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf, which a renderer on a host
without dma-buf cannot. The branch beside it already backs a blob with host
memory the renderer imports into native Vulkan, which is the same guarantee
the hardware buffer path needs: the guest never exports a native dma-buf,
it hands the renderer a virtio-gpu resource.

Offer the handle type there too, so the Android loader's image format query
is answered instead of refused and a swapchain can reach the driver.
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
index cad47760ad53f58501c18c07871b1d3a5ee703c5..a9d6c71142e913edd8e8d9d3e772a8813ee56b97 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
@@ -1090,9 +1090,14 @@ vn_physical_device_init_external_memory(
        */
       physical_dev->external_memory.renderer_handle_type =
          VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_HOST_ALLOCATION_BIT_EXT;
+#ifdef VK_USE_PLATFORM_ANDROID_KHR
+      physical_dev->external_memory.supported_handle_types |=
+         VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_ANDROID_HARDWARE_BUFFER_BIT_ANDROID;
+#else
       physical_dev->external_memory.supported_handle_types =
          VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_OPAQUE_FD_BIT |
          VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_DMA_BUF_BIT_EXT;
+#endif
       if (physical_dev->external_memory.renderer_supports_metal_heap) {
          physical_dev->external_memory.renderer_optimal_image_handle_type =
             VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_MTLHEAP_BIT_EXT;
